# FleetLink Performance Standards

## Golden Rule

Optimize for perceived performance and smooth UX first. Measure before micro-optimizing.

## Re-render Prevention

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — new object every render causes child re-render
<TripCard style={{ marginBottom: 16 }} trip={trip} />

// ✅ GOOD — styles in separate file, stable references
<TripCard trip={trip} />
```

- Do not pass inline objects, arrays, or arrow functions to memoized children.
- Lift state down — keep state as close to where it's needed as possible.
- Split large screens into smaller components so state changes affect fewer nodes.
- Use `React.memo` only when profiling or logic shows a measurable benefit — not by default.

## Memoization Guidelines

| Hook | Use when | Skip when |
|------|----------|-----------|
| `useMemo` | Expensive computation (filter/sort 1000+ items) | Simple string concat, trivial math |
| `useCallback` | Passed to memoized child or used in effect deps | Handler only used in same component's JSX |
| `React.memo` | Pure component re-renders often with same props | Component always gets new props |

**Default: no memoization.** Add it when you observe a problem.

## Lists — FlashList Required

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<FlatList data={trips} renderItem={...} />

// ✅ GOOD
<FlashList
  data={trips}
  renderItem={renderTrip}
  estimatedItemSize={80}
  keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}
  onEndReached={fetchNextPage}
  onEndReachedThreshold={0.5}
/>
```

- Use `@shopify/flash-list` for any list that may exceed 20 items.
- Always provide `estimatedItemSize`.
- Always provide stable `keyExtractor`.
- Extract `renderItem` with `useCallback` when passed to FlashList.

## Pagination & Data Loading

- Server-driven pagination for all list endpoints (`page`, `limit`, `total`).
- React Query `useInfiniteQuery` for infinite scroll lists.
- Prefetch next page when user is near the end.
- Debounce search inputs (300ms minimum) — never fire API on every keystroke.
- Cancel in-flight requests on unmount or query change (React Query handles this; ensure `signal` passed in Axios for manual calls).

## Navigation Performance

- Use React Navigation's native stack for primary flows.
- Lazy-load heavy screens with dynamic import where supported.
- Do not mount heavy modals/lists until opened.
- Cache inactive screens when back-navigation is frequent (default stack behavior).
- Avoid passing large objects through route params — pass IDs, fetch in screen hook.

## Images & Assets

- Use appropriately sized images. No full-resolution photos in list thumbnails.
- Prefer `expo-image` with caching for remote images.
- Lazy-load non-critical images below the fold.

## Network

- React Query `staleTime` and `gcTime` tuned per data type:
  - Static config: 30 min stale
  - Lists: 1–5 min stale
  - Real-time data (driver location): 0 stale, polling or WebSocket
- Background refetch on app focus (`refetchOnWindowFocus: true` for mobile app state).
- Batch related requests where the API supports it — avoid waterfall fetches.

## MMKV for Sync Reads

- Auth tokens, theme preference, onboarding flags → MMKV (synchronous, no flash).
- Never block render waiting for AsyncStorage.

## Performance Review Checklist

Before shipping a screen:

- [ ] Lists use FlashList with pagination
- [ ] No inline styles or inline object props on list items
- [ ] Search is debounced
- [ ] Heavy screens are not eagerly loaded
- [ ] React Query cache config is appropriate
- [ ] No `console.log` in production paths

## Anti-Patterns

| Pattern | Problem |
|---------|---------|
| `useMemo` everywhere | Noise, maintenance cost |
| Fetching in `useEffect` without React Query | No cache, no retry, no cancellation |
| Rendering 500 items without virtualization | Jank |
| Polling every 1s when 30s suffices | Battery + server load |
| Storing entire API response in Zustand | Duplicates React Query cache |
